abstract: "Word-timed, speaker-annotated machine transcripts of every Nixon White House conversation released as an individual recording (19,426 conversations, 2,206 hours), produced with a speech recognizer fine-tuned on the tapes, a second independent recognizer and archive-informed correction. Transcripts and model weights are CC BY 4.0; code is MIT."
keywords:
  - speech recognition
  - Nixon tapes
  - Watergate
  - presidential recordings
  - digital humanities
